{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfAHSPR6Uc4HzWxyBKtbg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I submitted **index 12 (Sb fraction 0.411)** as the best composition. It had an EQE of **0.840%**, the highest of the five I measured.\n\n| Index | Sb fraction | EQE (%) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 6 | 0.242 | 0.240 |\n| **12** | **0.411** | **0.840** |\n| 13 | 0.448 | 0.824 |\n| 15 | 0.519 | 0.771 |\n| 20 | 0.675 | 0.013 |\n\n- **Where the peak is:** EQE is high and fairly flat from about 0.41 to 0.52 Sb, and drops off sharply on both sides.\n- **My first guess was wrong:** I started at index 20 (Sb 0.675) because it sits closest to the known NiSb₂O₆ compound. It came out almost zero, so the best region is on the Ni-rich side of that composition.\n- **How I narrowed it down:** I measured indices 12, 6 and 15 to bracket the peak. I then fitted a curve through the results, which put the maximum near 0.44 Sb. Index 13 was at that spot but measured slightly lower than index 12.\n- **What wasn't measured:** Index 11 (Sb 0.379) and index 14 (Sb 0.485) are untested and could be slightly better. All five EQE measurements are used.\n- **XRD:** I didn't use any of the 5 XRD measurements. I chose compositions from the EQE results alone, so there's no confirmation of which crystal phases are present in the best films."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":491,"cache_read_input_tokens":7719,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":491},"output_tokens":512,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7e0f1bbe-5ff6-445b-ad89-989b71333127","uuid":"cecdc06a-0ce9-4191-ada4-6ecc5fff8554","timestamp":"2026-09-18T04:36:25.013Z","request_id":"req_011CfAHSNtbaR3wKZ4Wb27tM"}
